usage: orchestrator.py [-h] [--scenario SCENARIO] [--profile PROFILE]
                       [--runs RUNS] [--config CONFIG] [--profiles PROFILES]
                       [--db DB] [--interface INTERFACE] [--egress-only]
                       [--ingress-profile INGRESS_PROFILE] [--report REPORT]
                       [--list-scenarios] [--list-profiles] [--capture-pcap]
                       [--capture-filter CAPTURE_FILTER]
                       [--capture-dir CAPTURE_DIR] [--capture-loopback]
                       [--no-capture-loopback]
                       [--capture-loopback-filter CAPTURE_LOOPBACK_FILTER]
                       [--capture-l7] [--capture-l7-dir CAPTURE_L7_DIR]
                       [--capture-l7-hosts CAPTURE_L7_HOSTS]
                       [--capture-l7-proxy-port CAPTURE_L7_PROXY_PORT]
                       [--capture-l7-web-port CAPTURE_L7_WEB_PORT]
                       [--mcp-transport {stdio,http}]
                       [--run-timeout RUN_TIMEOUT] [--stop-on-error]
                       [--resume]

6G AI Traffic Characterization Testbed

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --scenario SCENARIO, -s SCENARIO
                        Scenario to run (or 'all' for test matrix)
  --profile PROFILE, -p PROFILE
                        Network profile to use
  --runs RUNS, -r RUNS  Number of runs per experiment
  --config CONFIG       Path to scenarios config
  --profiles PROFILES   Path to network profiles config
  --db DB               Path to SQLite database
  --interface INTERFACE
                        Network interface for emulation (auto = detect from
                        default route)
  --egress-only         Disable ingress shaping (only shape egress/outbound
                        traffic)
  --ingress-profile INGRESS_PROFILE
                        Use a different network profile for ingress traffic
                        (default: same as --profile)
  --report REPORT       Output path for report
  --list-scenarios      List available scenarios
  --list-profiles       List available network profiles
  --capture-pcap        Enable L3/L4 capture using tcpdump
  --capture-filter CAPTURE_FILTER
                        tcpdump filter expression. The default captures
                        HTTP(S) plus WebRTC ICE/SRTP/RTP UDP traffic. Pass an
                        empty string to capture all traffic.
  --capture-dir CAPTURE_DIR
                        Directory for pcap captures
  --capture-loopback    When MCP transport is http, also capture loopback (lo)
                        so MCP JSON-RPC frames are visible in pcap. Enabled by
                        default. Use --no-capture-loopback to disable.
  --no-capture-loopback
                        Disable the secondary loopback capture (mirror flag).
  --capture-loopback-filter CAPTURE_LOOPBACK_FILTER
                        BPF filter for the loopback capture. Defaults to 'not
                        port 22 and not port 53'.
  --capture-l7          Enable L7 capture using mitmproxy
  --capture-l7-dir CAPTURE_L7_DIR
                        Directory for L7 captures
  --capture-l7-hosts CAPTURE_L7_HOSTS
                        Comma-separated hostnames to filter L7 capture
  --capture-l7-proxy-port CAPTURE_L7_PROXY_PORT
                        Port for mitmproxy
  --capture-l7-web-port CAPTURE_L7_WEB_PORT
                        Port for mitmproxy web UI (0 to disable)
  --mcp-transport {stdio,http}
                        MCP server transport: stdio (pipe, no netem) or http
                        (TCP, netem-shaped)
  --run-timeout RUN_TIMEOUT
                        Per-run timeout in seconds (default: no timeout).
                        Individual runs that exceed this are marked as failed
                        and skipped.
  --stop-on-error       Stop immediately on the first failed run (after
                        retries).
  --resume              Resume from where a previous run left off. Skips
                        scenario/profile combinations that already have enough
                        successful runs in the database.
